  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given NNN pairs of integers. The iii-th pair is denoted (Ai,Bi)(A_i, B_i)(Ai​,Bi​).\n\nIt's guaranteed that Ai≤BiA_i \\le B_iAi​≤Bi​ for every 1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N.\n\nFor an integer XXX, we define f(X)f(X)f(X) to be the result of the following process:\n\n\nLet YYY be a variable.\n\nInitially, Y=XY = XY=X.\nFor each i=1,2,…,Ni = 1, 2, \\ldots, Ni=1,2,…,N **in order**,\n\nIf Y&lt;AiY \\lt A_iY&lt;Ai​, set Y=AiY = A_iY=Ai​.\nIf Y&gt;BiY \\gt B_iY&gt;Bi​, set Y=BiY = B_iY=Bi​.\nIf Ai≤Y≤BiA_i \\le Y \\le B_iAi​≤Y≤Bi​, the value of YYY doesn't change.\n\n\nf(X)f(X)f(X) is defined to be the final value of YYY after all NNN steps of the process have been performed.\n\nYour task is to find the **maximum possible value** of f(X)f(X)f(X) across all possible input integers XXX.\n\nIt can be proved that this value is finite.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the number of pairs of integers.\nThe next NNN lines describe the pairs. The iii-th of these NNN lines contains two space-separated integers AiA_iAi​ and BiB_iBi​, denoting the elements of the iii-th pair.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the answer: the maximum possible value of f(X)f(X)f(X) across all integers XXX.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤1001 \\leq N \\leq 1001≤N≤100",
      "1≤Ai≤Bi≤1001 \\le A_i \\le B_i \\le 1001≤Ai​≤Bi​≤100"
    ],
